 "about": "Words that assistant rewrites of people's drafts add (positive weight) or remove (negative weight). Learned from 6553 pairs of a human draft and an assistant rewrite of it (asks to polish it, make it a LinkedIn post, make it punchier, make it more professional or fill out a rough draft; three model families), over 12 writing domains: Stack Exchange answers from eight non-code sites, company blog excerpts, a writer's own posts, office email and forum posts, all written before November 2022. Each weight is the log-odds of a word being added rather than removed, with a prior; a word must change in at least 5 sources across at least 3 domains, and names are left out. The list is learned on all of those pairs; held-out numbers for it come from lists learned without the text being scored.",
